 ## Ordinary equipment loot quality

-The October 18 rule values are 2000 Polished, 500 Exalted and 100 Ascended out of 10000. A single roll applies to each eligible, newly generated ordinary equipment or bag drop. A missing quality variant falls back to the base item. Zone Hunt, instance rewards and quest turn-ins have separate policies.
-
-The deployed November 27 `NPC::AddLootDrop` policy in `server-mods/code/zone/loot.cpp` adds three times the existing Ascended band from otherwise Normal rolls only for equippable common armor and shields (item types 10 and 8). At the live baseline this gives 4% Ascended armor and shields and 1% for other eligible items. Both have 20% Polished and 5% Exalted. The override values themselves stay at 2000/500/100. This code requires the matching zone executable and fresh NPC loot. `tools/tests/test_loot_quality_rates.py` exhausts all rolls, and `wiki/loot_model.py` mirrors the model using captured itemclass, itemtype and slots. The public Loot Finder now uses the matching worker. Its HTTPS snapshot verified the Runnyeye armor and Hole weapon controls. Main 58e14d9b, LocalDev and OVH deployment verified November 27. All 12 OVH zone workers passed. Player acceptance is open. See docs/releases/classic-qa-20261127/QA.md and ops/production-verified.json in that release.
+The November 27 seven-percent release uses the native zone rule on all newly generated ordinary equippable item and bag drops. Ruleset 1 on LocalDev and OVH has Zone:LootTierLegendaryChance=700, Zone:LootTierEpicChance=500 and Zone:LootTierRareChance=2000 out of 10,000. All variants present gives 7% Ascended, 5% Exalted, 20% Polished and 68% Normal. The same roll applies to armor, shields, weapons, jewelry and bags. The server leaves a missing selected variant on its base item. Previously generated loot, the separate Hunt and dungeon pools, direct grants and forging retain their existing behavior.
+
+Main bd478e11b pairs the zone binary from gameplay source 4901749f9 with the PEQ rule. No client update is needed. server-mods/code/zone/loot.cpp and tools/tests/test_loot_quality_rates.py implement and exhaust the native roll. eq-solo-gm/scripts/tiered_loot_setup.sql supplies the setup value. wiki/loot_model.py projects the effective rule for each NPC source. See docs/releases/ascended-seven-20261127/ for the guarded rollout and tests. In-game player QA is open.
+

